1
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:05,147
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

2
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:05,627
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

3
00:00:05,947 --> 00:00:28,433
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you aren't speaking, there's thoughts and then there's this domain of speech that you haven't broken out into, you haven't started speaking.

4
00:00:28,893 --> 00:00:29,793
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that seems different.

5
00:00:31,513 --> 00:00:32,294
[SPEAKER_00]: What's different?

6
00:00:32,654 --> 00:00:34,676
[SPEAKER_00]: The domain of speech, the domain of thought.

7
00:00:36,577 --> 00:00:39,419
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

8
00:00:42,461 --> 00:00:53,109
[SPEAKER_00]: But if speech and thought are fundamentally different, then that would mean that when you're speaking, there's also thinking.

9
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:54,830
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, of course.

10
00:00:55,311 --> 00:00:56,892
[SPEAKER_00]: That the speech isn't

11
00:00:58,357 --> 00:00:58,857
[SPEAKER_00]: In place.

12
00:00:59,018 --> 00:01:02,521
[SPEAKER_00]: In place of the thoughts, yes.

13
00:01:05,303 --> 00:01:14,051
[SPEAKER_01]: But how about when you're not speaking, but thinking to speak, but you're not actually uttering any sounds?

14
00:01:15,192 --> 00:01:16,113
[SPEAKER_01]: Is there a problem with that?

15
00:01:21,387 --> 00:01:23,628
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, is there still some sort of assumption in the...

16
00:01:23,648 --> 00:01:27,729
[SPEAKER_00]: There's still an assumption that you can enter the body with the mind.

17
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:30,951
[SPEAKER_00]: You can, you know, like, eh...

18
00:01:31,911 --> 00:01:32,131
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

19
00:01:32,171 --> 00:01:33,672
[SPEAKER_01]: Make the body... Yeah.

20
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:34,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you can sort of...

21
00:01:35,072 --> 00:01:36,073
[SPEAKER_01]: Enter the will of the mind.

22
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:40,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Pretty much like a linear, almost... Yeah.

23
00:01:40,574 --> 00:01:45,036
[SPEAKER_00]: Channeling of your... of your thought into your speech.

24
00:01:45,176 --> 00:01:45,396
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

25
00:01:45,436 --> 00:01:49,898
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're basically assuming that you can take up... Hmm.

26
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:55,855
[SPEAKER_00]: With thoughts, yeah.

27
00:01:56,675 --> 00:02:00,318
[SPEAKER_00]: Actually, kind of, enter the mouth, enter the body.

28
00:02:00,358 --> 00:02:00,718
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

29
00:02:00,738 --> 00:02:10,485
[SPEAKER_01]: You just sort of... any form of identifying it, to whatever extent, to that extent, it's a problem.

30
00:02:11,526 --> 00:02:14,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's a contradiction in terms.

31
00:02:15,188 --> 00:02:18,350
[SPEAKER_01]: But say you're not speaking, you're not saying anything, so you're practicing silence.

32
00:02:19,251 --> 00:02:20,472
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not actually saying anything.

33
00:02:22,290 --> 00:02:23,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Your mind, obviously, is always thinking.

34
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:26,091
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what mind does, has thoughts.

35
00:02:28,332 --> 00:02:33,954
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, taking up of the mouth, of the verbal domain.

36
00:02:36,234 --> 00:02:38,355
[SPEAKER_01]: Is that done solely through speaking?

37
00:02:38,515 --> 00:02:40,436
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can do that even while you're being silent?

38
00:02:41,436 --> 00:02:42,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's the thing.

39
00:02:42,616 --> 00:02:45,857
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's different kinds of thinking.

40
00:02:46,417 --> 00:02:47,818
[SPEAKER_00]: There's sort of...

41
00:02:50,932 --> 00:02:56,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Thinking, like verbal thinking, thinking where you're kind of thinking in words.

42
00:02:58,378 --> 00:02:58,718
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay?

43
00:02:59,699 --> 00:03:03,161
[SPEAKER_00]: So, can you think in words without taking up your mouth?

44
00:03:03,341 --> 00:03:06,344
[SPEAKER_00]: It seems to me, no.

45
00:03:06,744 --> 00:03:11,828
[SPEAKER_00]: Because those thoughts are what they are, because of that, the way the mouth works.

46
00:03:12,827 --> 00:03:13,047
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

47
00:03:13,147 --> 00:03:18,928
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can then... you can start to see the difference between your thinking and your thinking that's taking up the mouth.

48
00:03:21,729 --> 00:03:24,910
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how... how do you then not take up the mouth?

49
00:03:30,071 --> 00:03:38,393
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, let me ask you like this.

50
00:03:39,573 --> 00:03:40,513
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you take up the mouth?

51
00:03:43,275 --> 00:03:50,500
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, well, fundamentally now, that you take up the mouth by assuming that you can take up the mouth.

52
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:50,760
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

53
00:03:52,802 --> 00:03:54,383
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, how do you not take up the mouth?

54
00:03:54,843 --> 00:03:56,925
[SPEAKER_00]: By understanding that you can't take up the mouth.

55
00:03:57,145 --> 00:03:57,325
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

56
00:03:57,405 --> 00:04:02,669
[SPEAKER_01]: By not losing the context of this body, of the mouth, untakeable.

57
00:04:02,789 --> 00:04:03,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Untakeable.

58
00:04:03,449 --> 00:04:03,690
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

59
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:04,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Literally.

60
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:08,793
[SPEAKER_01]: Completely beyond my... all anything I could possibly think about.

61
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:09,814
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is no

62
00:04:11,478 --> 00:04:13,739
[SPEAKER_01]: And this is true for putujana and for anarahant.

63
00:04:13,839 --> 00:04:17,700
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no speaking without taking up the mouth with your thought.

64
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:24,061
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, there is no grabbing things with your hand without taking up your hand with your mind.

65
00:04:24,262 --> 00:04:24,982
[SPEAKER_01]: But surely...

66
00:04:25,242 --> 00:04:26,462
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that would be the same.

67
00:04:26,902 --> 00:04:34,124
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, there's no walking across the room without taking up your body, without the body becoming...

68
00:04:34,144 --> 00:04:37,785
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you sort of take the body mentally as the way across the room.

69
00:04:37,985 --> 00:04:38,185
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

70
00:04:39,566 --> 00:04:40,106
[SPEAKER_00]: But surely,

71
00:04:41,147 --> 00:04:45,989
[SPEAKER_00]: An arahant could do... walk across the room without taking up the body.

72
00:04:46,109 --> 00:04:46,489
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

73
00:04:46,629 --> 00:04:48,630
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, see, that's what I'm trying to point out here.

74
00:04:49,150 --> 00:04:50,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Taking up does not mean assuming.

75
00:04:51,011 --> 00:04:51,911
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, right, right, right.

76
00:04:51,991 --> 00:04:52,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

77
00:04:52,331 --> 00:04:55,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Taking up literally means bodily intention.

78
00:04:55,092 --> 00:04:55,852
[SPEAKER_01]: Borrowing, borrowing, using.

79
00:04:55,872 --> 00:04:58,333
[SPEAKER_01]: You... verbal intention, mental intention.

80
00:04:59,274 --> 00:04:59,574
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you...

81
00:04:59,594 --> 00:05:00,114
[SPEAKER_01]: Determining.

82
00:05:00,274 --> 00:05:01,795
[SPEAKER_01]: Taking up means determining it.

83
00:05:01,895 --> 00:05:04,396
[SPEAKER_00]: You can sort of use... Can we say that, like?

84
00:05:04,436 --> 00:05:05,856
[SPEAKER_00]: You can sort of use... No.

85
00:05:05,896 --> 00:05:06,356
[SPEAKER_00]: ...the body.

86
00:05:06,376 --> 00:05:07,877
[SPEAKER_01]: ...usage disorder after you've taken up.

87
00:05:10,062 --> 00:05:12,004
[SPEAKER_01]: Taking up is intending upon it.

88
00:05:12,364 --> 00:05:12,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

89
00:05:12,624 --> 00:05:12,885
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

90
00:05:12,965 --> 00:05:15,007
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you intend upon the body, basically.

91
00:05:15,027 --> 00:05:16,308
[SPEAKER_01]: To that extent, you took it up.

92
00:05:16,508 --> 00:05:21,212
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you can walk, sit, move, whatever, extend your limbs.

93
00:05:21,252 --> 00:05:22,133
[SPEAKER_01]: Same with speaking.

94
00:05:22,193 --> 00:05:22,353
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

95
00:05:22,694 --> 00:05:27,078
[SPEAKER_01]: But speaking, it's as you said before, it's a more particular way of taking up the body.

96
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:27,378
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

97
00:05:27,979 --> 00:05:29,720
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's a verbal taking up of the body.

98
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:30,661
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

99
00:05:31,402 --> 00:05:32,543
[SPEAKER_01]: And the same works for the mind.

100
00:05:33,318 --> 00:05:38,583
[SPEAKER_01]: Mental intention is the taking up of the mind, of that which is the thoughts, the ideas that have presented themselves.

101
00:05:38,603 --> 00:05:38,863
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

102
00:05:38,883 --> 00:05:45,829
[SPEAKER_00]: There seems to be a closer link between the body and the mind and that speech bit.

103
00:05:47,005 --> 00:05:47,685
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

104
00:05:47,725 --> 00:05:48,546
[SPEAKER_01]: But I would say that even...

105
00:05:48,606 --> 00:05:49,506
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the same principle.

106
00:05:49,786 --> 00:05:50,126
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

107
00:05:50,146 --> 00:05:54,268
[SPEAKER_01]: When you walk, when you move across the room, you're doing it because you want to do it.

108
00:05:54,368 --> 00:05:55,848
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a mental intention.

109
00:05:55,948 --> 00:06:02,791
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, by the way, the reason why it seems to be a closer link is because you've been practicing physical restraint for a number of years now.

110
00:06:03,051 --> 00:06:09,353
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you taking up the body as a... out of habit, has been sort of suppressed long time ago.

111
00:06:09,373 --> 00:06:13,735
[SPEAKER_01]: Or as the Buddha would say that a behavior has been purified well beforehand.

112
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:15,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

113
00:06:15,789 --> 00:06:18,250
[SPEAKER_01]: But yes, now it's time to do that with the mouth.

114
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:18,650
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

115
00:06:19,911 --> 00:06:22,432
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, eventually, you'll be able to do that on the level of the mind.

116
00:06:22,452 --> 00:06:26,094
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, yes, there is no problem in any domain, because that's where everything was rooted.

117
00:06:27,634 --> 00:06:32,857
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is to recognize that taking up of the mouth is how you speak.

118
00:06:33,866 --> 00:06:36,007
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot speak without taking up the mouth.

119
00:06:36,428 --> 00:06:46,173
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how can you... what you want to learn, discern, is taking up the mouth, but without assuming the identity of the verbal domain and mental domain.

120
00:06:47,114 --> 00:06:53,418
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what I'm saying is, you want to recognize that taking up does not automatically mean assumption.

121
00:06:53,438 --> 00:06:57,180
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you recognize that?

122
00:07:07,357 --> 00:07:07,978
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop speaking.

123
00:07:08,458 --> 00:07:09,438
[SPEAKER_01]: Restrain your speech.

124
00:07:10,579 --> 00:07:13,540
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop speaking in the sense of don't engage in an unwholesome speech.

125
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,520
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

126
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,481
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is...

127
00:07:15,521 --> 00:07:15,921
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

128
00:07:15,961 --> 00:07:19,302
[SPEAKER_01]: Which then extends to the point of speaking without a purpose.

129
00:07:19,442 --> 00:07:22,103
[SPEAKER_01]: It's unwholesome for the development of the mind.

130
00:07:22,203 --> 00:07:23,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Sampapalapa.

131
00:07:23,023 --> 00:07:25,725
[SPEAKER_00]: That's one of the aspects of wrong speech.

132
00:07:25,825 --> 00:07:26,605
[SPEAKER_00]: Speaking nonsense.

133
00:07:26,645 --> 00:07:27,645
[SPEAKER_00]: Speaking... Yeah.

134
00:07:27,925 --> 00:07:28,326
[SPEAKER_00]: Trivial.

135
00:07:28,606 --> 00:07:28,946
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

136
00:07:28,986 --> 00:07:29,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Trivial.

137
00:07:29,966 --> 00:07:31,847
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you then speak when needed.

138
00:07:32,807 --> 00:07:34,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again, speaking is not a problem.

139
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:45,136
[SPEAKER_01]: But the problem is that you can't differentiate it from assuming the identity of the verbal and mental domain, merging, same, different, whatever, being confused about it.

140
00:07:45,296 --> 00:07:53,622
[SPEAKER_01]: So, taking up of speech means taking up of the body for you, taking up of everything bodily, which means then you're subjected to everything bodily, to the hindrances, namely.

141
00:07:54,282 --> 00:07:56,463
[SPEAKER_01]: You take up the whole body by taking up speech.

142
00:07:56,483 --> 00:07:56,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

143
00:07:56,824 --> 00:08:03,308
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why if you practice jhānas, the... we said like mindfulness of non-speaking,

144
00:08:03,978 --> 00:08:10,022
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, mindfulness of the mouth that hasn't been taken up, is what mindfulness of the body is at the time for you there.

145
00:08:10,242 --> 00:08:18,506
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's just more specific type of mindfulness of the body, like being there, discerning the extent of the bodily domain.

146
00:08:19,813 --> 00:08:23,016
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you undermine your own sense of ownership of it.

147
00:08:23,096 --> 00:08:26,218
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize there is no before or after this, or above or below.

148
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:28,880
[SPEAKER_01]: I am within it and I cannot step outside of it.

149
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:38,528
[SPEAKER_01]: And the extent of it, it doesn't matter how far it goes, how near it comes, can never enter me, as in my mind and my thoughts can never enter it.

150
00:08:38,588 --> 00:08:41,110
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always these two simultaneous things present there together.

151
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:41,450
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

152
00:08:43,112 --> 00:08:45,794
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in order to...

153
00:08:48,508 --> 00:09:00,817
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's say, in order to understand what jhāna is, to dwell, having... having jhāna manifested, let's say.

154
00:09:00,857 --> 00:09:01,017
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

155
00:09:01,617 --> 00:09:09,923
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is basically the imperturbable image of the correct extent of that body.

156
00:09:10,264 --> 00:09:10,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

157
00:09:12,846 --> 00:09:14,727
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the sense of safety that comes from it.

158
00:09:15,868 --> 00:09:16,928
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't lose anything.

159
00:09:17,268 --> 00:09:23,630
[SPEAKER_01]: Any disturbance is within this extent that now I see fully in its nature.

160
00:09:28,471 --> 00:09:43,994
[SPEAKER_00]: So it begins by, you know, you said before, it begins by understanding the extent of the sensual domain and by overcoming

161
00:09:46,172 --> 00:09:55,280
[SPEAKER_00]: Making yourself safe from the hindrances, which involves mindfulness of the body.

162
00:10:00,544 --> 00:10:09,572
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, and so understanding the body to the extent that... What is the absolute root, then, of safety from hindrances?

163
00:10:12,981 --> 00:10:14,222
[SPEAKER_01]: Something you're responsible for.

164
00:10:15,102 --> 00:10:21,886
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, not acting out of... Sure, but more, more specifically, more accurately than that.

165
00:10:22,547 --> 00:10:24,748
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, what is a necessary basis for you acting out?

166
00:10:25,668 --> 00:10:26,729
[SPEAKER_00]: By body or by speech?

167
00:10:27,810 --> 00:10:29,050
[SPEAKER_00]: By taking ownership of the body.

168
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:29,851
[SPEAKER_00]: Taking it up.

169
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:30,351
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

170
00:10:30,651 --> 00:10:35,314
[SPEAKER_01]: Not, not necessarily... Yeah, it's ownership, of course, but you don't need to think in terms of ownership.

171
00:10:35,354 --> 00:10:36,835
[SPEAKER_01]: You're just taking it up because you can.

172
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:37,455
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

173
00:10:39,147 --> 00:10:47,638
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you learn how to not take it up, while it's there enduring on its own, means there is no basis for hindrance to basically pertain to you, turn to you.

174
00:10:47,778 --> 00:10:47,958
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

175
00:10:48,739 --> 00:10:51,323
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the practice of jhāna, then, is practice of not taking up.

176
00:10:51,864 --> 00:10:52,064
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

177
00:10:52,164 --> 00:10:56,429
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, first of all, you might say, you begin by not taking up the body.

178
00:10:57,254 --> 00:11:01,698
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, then the body becomes this more particular aspect of the body.

179
00:11:02,219 --> 00:11:02,419
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

180
00:11:02,439 --> 00:11:02,699
[SPEAKER_01]: Speech.

181
00:11:02,999 --> 00:11:06,483
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but just while you were still at it, you see, you begin.

182
00:11:06,563 --> 00:11:07,003
[SPEAKER_01]: That's true.

183
00:11:07,323 --> 00:11:13,129
[SPEAKER_01]: We have to be careful because in the beginning, you not taking up the body is what you take up.

184
00:11:13,149 --> 00:11:14,069
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

185
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:18,073
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to start thinking about the ways of not taking up the body.

186
00:11:18,193 --> 00:11:18,393
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

187
00:11:18,634 --> 00:11:21,676
[SPEAKER_01]: But it takes time until you start discerning body on its own terms.

188
00:11:21,697 --> 00:11:21,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

189
00:11:22,437 --> 00:11:24,378
[SPEAKER_01]: Which then manifests as... As something that can't be taken up.

190
00:11:24,438 --> 00:11:24,978
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

191
00:11:25,178 --> 00:11:26,058
[SPEAKER_01]: As not being taken up.

192
00:11:26,198 --> 00:11:31,080
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you're not clear about it, and it's certainly if you're acting out of your craving, you will be...

193
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I'm not taking up.

194
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,880
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not taking up.

195
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:36,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is your very extreme way of taking it up.

196
00:11:37,462 --> 00:11:41,443
[SPEAKER_01]: So, taking up is kind of a matter of your choice.

197
00:11:42,043 --> 00:11:43,224
[SPEAKER_01]: Not taking up isn't.

198
00:11:44,164 --> 00:11:47,165
[SPEAKER_01]: Not taking up is basically removing the basis for taking up

199
00:11:47,729 --> 00:11:50,354
[SPEAKER_01]: That then results in the experience of not taking it up.

200
00:11:51,156 --> 00:11:54,363
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the removing for basis of taking up the body is sīla.

201
00:11:55,770 --> 00:11:58,292
[SPEAKER_01]: Keeping sīla removes the basis of taking up the body.

202
00:11:58,813 --> 00:12:02,376
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you can get to understand how to not take it up, in that negative sense.

203
00:12:02,456 --> 00:12:03,276
[SPEAKER_01]: Same with speaking.

204
00:12:03,297 --> 00:12:07,320
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why I said, like, it's... you're mindful of the fact that the mouth is not speaking.

205
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:22,053
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no voice being uttered, sound being... there is no communication or expression, which means now, if there is any taking up, it's not being perpetuated by the actual acts on the verbal domain, but they're only in the attitude of your mind.

206
00:12:22,293 --> 00:12:23,374
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where you can see it.

207
00:12:23,754 --> 00:12:28,238
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can't see it on the level of your mind as an attitude of taking up while you're talking.

208
00:12:29,018 --> 00:12:33,422
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, you can't see on the level of your mind the attitude of sensuality while you're engaging in sensuality.

209
00:12:33,542 --> 00:12:34,042
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

210
00:12:40,687 --> 00:12:45,331
[SPEAKER_00]: So, taking up simply means determining.

211
00:12:46,504 --> 00:12:51,146
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and practically what it means, means thinking about it, in a way.

212
00:12:51,826 --> 00:12:57,609
[SPEAKER_01]: See, the only way you take up your mouth is literally by having a thought of taking it up.

213
00:12:57,649 --> 00:12:57,909
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

214
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:04,711
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no other way that's hidden from you than the ways you take up your mouth.

215
00:13:04,731 --> 00:13:08,773
[SPEAKER_00]: For as long as there's a possibility to take up the mouth, you've taken it up.

216
00:13:10,013 --> 00:13:10,213
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

217
00:13:10,394 --> 00:13:11,495
[SPEAKER_01]: And, as I said, that's not the problem.

218
00:13:11,956 --> 00:13:16,222
[SPEAKER_01]: You thinking about the mouth, as in, I'm about to speak or I want to say something, that's not the problem.

219
00:13:16,642 --> 00:13:19,446
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is the significance of that thought of taking up your mouth.

220
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:20,347
[SPEAKER_01]: You haven't understood it.

221
00:13:20,888 --> 00:13:22,811
[SPEAKER_00]: So, for you, that thought carries the assumption.

222
00:13:23,231 --> 00:13:26,896
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the possibility of taking up the mouth is because...

223
00:13:29,373 --> 00:13:33,137
[SPEAKER_00]: I can mentally manipulate... Well, I can speak.

224
00:13:33,397 --> 00:13:33,937
[SPEAKER_01]: I can speak.

225
00:13:34,478 --> 00:13:36,540
[SPEAKER_01]: And I seem to say things and people seem to hear them.

226
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,701
[SPEAKER_01]: So, my speech is real.

227
00:13:38,381 --> 00:13:39,202
[SPEAKER_01]: My voice is real.

228
00:13:39,602 --> 00:13:41,184
[SPEAKER_01]: Me taking up the mouth is real.

229
00:13:41,724 --> 00:13:43,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, I am taking it up because I can.

230
00:13:45,307 --> 00:13:46,248
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's never the problem.

231
00:13:46,489 --> 00:13:49,872
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is that that also means you're assuming the ownership of it.

232
00:13:50,962 --> 00:13:52,483
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how can you take it up without owning it?

233
00:13:52,563 --> 00:13:54,625
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you take it up without confusing the two domains?

234
00:13:54,645 --> 00:13:59,508
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you take it up without identifying your thought with your speech or or interchanging and whatever else?

235
00:13:59,828 --> 00:14:01,349
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I understand.

236
00:14:01,429 --> 00:14:02,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

237
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:09,996
[SPEAKER_01]: By practicing restraint in regard to it and then by understanding the extent of that non-speaking mouth while it's being taken up mentally.

238
00:14:10,296 --> 00:14:10,396
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

239
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:18,602
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you actually get to stop taking it mentally because you realize that thought of the mouth cannot take up the mouth in that material sense that is being assumed.

240
00:14:18,622 --> 00:14:18,842
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

241
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:28,496
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's only a direction of the mind towards speech, but you can only break into speech from its own verbal domain, not from the domain of your thought.

242
00:14:31,138 --> 00:14:34,680
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why having thought and ponder, one breaks into speech.

243
00:14:40,264 --> 00:14:41,165
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you mean the...

244
00:14:45,547 --> 00:14:47,767
[SPEAKER_00]: The determinations for speech are not mental.

245
00:14:47,787 --> 00:14:48,708
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that what you're saying?

246
00:14:49,068 --> 00:14:49,968
[SPEAKER_00]: They're verbal.

247
00:14:50,048 --> 00:14:52,528
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a particular... there's these three domains.

248
00:14:54,329 --> 00:14:56,089
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I mean they're mental.

249
00:14:56,109 --> 00:14:58,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Determination for speech is mental.

250
00:14:58,050 --> 00:15:00,510
[SPEAKER_01]: Speech is verbal.

251
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:02,090
[SPEAKER_01]: Determination for speech is not verbal.

252
00:15:03,371 --> 00:15:04,931
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a determination for verbal.

253
00:15:08,912 --> 00:15:13,433
[SPEAKER_01]: So, determination for speech is basically the thought of the mouth that takes up the mouth.

254
00:15:15,077 --> 00:15:21,660
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, not specifically, I think, about the look of the mouth, but the mind comes down into this cavity, so to speak.

255
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:24,081
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, you want to grab something.

256
00:15:24,682 --> 00:15:26,262
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, your mind is in your hand.

257
00:15:26,603 --> 00:15:26,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

258
00:15:26,903 --> 00:15:27,083
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

259
00:15:27,283 --> 00:15:29,584
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, yeah, you've got... you're basically thinking about something.

260
00:15:29,764 --> 00:15:32,365
[SPEAKER_00]: But that has a shape of... that has some kind of bodily shape.

261
00:15:32,405 --> 00:15:32,725
[SPEAKER_00]: It does.

262
00:15:32,745 --> 00:15:34,806
[SPEAKER_00]: It's assumed on some extent of the body.

263
00:15:34,906 --> 00:15:44,291
[SPEAKER_01]: And see, that's already how you get to, like, how the... so to say, like, embody, as we spoke the other day, embody your personality view into the body, as if that's possible.

264
00:15:47,403 --> 00:15:55,546
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you stop assuming that your mind that's in your hand, when it's about to take something you want, is actually in your hand.

265
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:58,466
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you might say, oh, so my mind is not in my hand.

266
00:15:58,506 --> 00:16:00,207
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's another formulation between mind.

267
00:16:00,247 --> 00:16:01,607
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no relationship.

268
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:04,128
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the mind, there is the hand.

269
00:16:04,548 --> 00:16:09,170
[SPEAKER_01]: And the sense of space that's revealed, basically, by the body, but it's secondary already to that mind.

270
00:16:10,890 --> 00:16:15,772
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you want to speak, can you speak without placing your mind, again, so to speak, in your mouth?

271
00:16:16,610 --> 00:16:16,990
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't.

272
00:16:17,811 --> 00:16:19,872
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the necessary condition for speech.

273
00:16:20,552 --> 00:16:21,893
[SPEAKER_01]: The necessary determination.

274
00:16:22,513 --> 00:16:23,234
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's a thought.

275
00:16:24,094 --> 00:16:26,215
[SPEAKER_01]: And whatever you're about to say, it's within that thought.

276
00:16:26,296 --> 00:16:28,937
[SPEAKER_01]: It's further of those thoughts.

277
00:16:30,438 --> 00:16:34,180
[SPEAKER_01]: But in the jhāna, you don't have that taking up of the mouth anymore.

278
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,621
[SPEAKER_01]: You have thinking and pondering.

279
00:16:36,701 --> 00:16:43,685
[SPEAKER_01]: But that embodying of those thoughts into the verbal cavity, that's not there.

280
00:16:43,926 --> 00:16:45,466
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why speech has subsided.

281
00:16:45,707 --> 00:16:46,167
[SPEAKER_01]: It ceased.

282
00:16:47,218 --> 00:16:47,978
[SPEAKER_01]: During that time.

283
00:16:48,418 --> 00:16:51,380
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, at that time, you're unable to take up the mouth.

284
00:16:54,601 --> 00:17:00,403
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you... that's the difference between somebody who is in the first jhāna and somebody who is simply not speaking anything verbally.

285
00:17:01,503 --> 00:17:13,028
[SPEAKER_01]: In his mind, through all of those verbal words and thoughts that you said, every of those, like, images and concepts that are verbalized, every verbalization

286
00:17:13,868 --> 00:17:15,949
[SPEAKER_01]: is habitually taking up the mouth.

287
00:17:16,589 --> 00:17:20,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Only you're not speaking, and that's good, because then you can get to discern it.

288
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:24,732
[SPEAKER_01]: Nevertheless, that's still not like that your determination for speech has ceased.

289
00:17:25,012 --> 00:17:25,252
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

290
00:17:27,493 --> 00:17:41,658
[SPEAKER_01]: But when those thoughts stop taking up of the of the of the verbal cavity of the mouth... Because you know that... Well, because that's another thought.

291
00:17:42,738 --> 00:17:42,938
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

292
00:17:45,491 --> 00:17:52,033
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it was your thoughts taking up your thoughts, but for you, some of those thoughts stood for the mouth, for the body.

293
00:17:55,713 --> 00:17:57,614
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, yeah, all you have is thinking and pondering.

294
00:17:57,694 --> 00:18:07,356
[SPEAKER_00]: So, but that's, that's the the funny thing, the strange thing, that we are we are skilled at manipulating the body.

295
00:18:07,376 --> 00:18:13,938
[SPEAKER_00]: We've somehow learned to speak, to, to, to basically

296
00:18:15,424 --> 00:18:18,006
[SPEAKER_00]: We've got this domain of thought and this domain of speech.

297
00:18:20,088 --> 00:18:24,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Two completely incompatible, separate... And domain of physical action.

298
00:18:26,734 --> 00:18:26,934
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

299
00:18:27,215 --> 00:18:28,596
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, they're not even incompatible.

300
00:18:28,676 --> 00:18:30,277
[SPEAKER_01]: They're not even incompatible.

301
00:18:31,458 --> 00:18:34,701
[SPEAKER_01]: Saying it's compatible, incompatible, it is a form of relationship.

302
00:18:34,801 --> 00:18:35,062
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

303
00:18:35,182 --> 00:18:36,623
[SPEAKER_01]: Relating them, comparing them.

304
00:18:36,963 --> 00:18:38,164
[SPEAKER_01]: They're invisible to each other.

305
00:18:38,945 --> 00:18:40,927
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's the... if they're invisible to each other,

306
00:18:41,857 --> 00:18:46,220
[SPEAKER_00]: It seems it's remarkable how we have learned how to walk, how to speak.

307
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:51,383
[SPEAKER_01]: It's remarkable if you come from your point of view first, but your point of view is not first.

308
00:18:53,004 --> 00:19:02,571
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's remarkable because the connection between these things escapes you, and it escapes you because it's actually fundamentally external to you, and thus inconceivable to you.

309
00:19:04,572 --> 00:19:05,473
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just how it is.

310
00:19:06,553 --> 00:19:06,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

311
00:19:07,194 --> 00:19:14,925
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the only sense you... the only reason you have a sense of self and I am and logic and the mind is because these things are there beforehand.

312
00:19:15,285 --> 00:19:15,525
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

313
00:19:15,766 --> 00:19:18,269
[SPEAKER_01]: The body, the verbal domain and the mental domain.

314
00:19:19,411 --> 00:19:20,091
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's...

315
00:19:20,131 --> 00:19:23,917
[SPEAKER_01]: But in order to... if like... if you were to be able to understand

316
00:19:24,814 --> 00:19:26,135
[SPEAKER_01]: How is thinking and pondering?

317
00:19:26,255 --> 00:19:30,019
[SPEAKER_01]: How the saṅkhara of it determines the speech, for example?

318
00:19:30,219 --> 00:19:34,563
[SPEAKER_01]: That would require you to step outside of yourself, to see how yourself works.

319
00:19:35,224 --> 00:19:41,770
[SPEAKER_01]: And that can only be conceived by somebody who has fully misconceived the sense of self, as something that comes first.

320
00:19:42,411 --> 00:19:46,374
[SPEAKER_01]: It's something that can even think these theoretical things to be addressed.

321
00:19:46,494 --> 00:19:46,835
[SPEAKER_01]: How?

322
00:19:47,865 --> 00:19:50,306
[SPEAKER_01]: When the sense of how is actually secondary already to that.

323
00:19:50,326 --> 00:19:54,308
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the Buddha, what he calls, sorry, by the invalid questions.

324
00:19:54,788 --> 00:19:54,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

325
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:56,469
[SPEAKER_01]: Not invalid, because I don't want to answer.

326
00:19:56,509 --> 00:19:58,250
[SPEAKER_01]: Invalid, because it's simply the wrong premise.

327
00:19:58,290 --> 00:19:58,770
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

328
00:19:58,790 --> 00:20:00,190
[SPEAKER_01]: Utterly based on the wrong premise.

329
00:20:00,411 --> 00:20:02,612
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, just not worth entertaining at all.

330
00:20:04,692 --> 00:20:11,275
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's say, when we learn skills, we learn how to speak, we learn how to walk or ride a bike or something.

331
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:14,877
[SPEAKER_00]: All we do, all we do is just kind of fumble.

332
00:20:16,695 --> 00:20:17,515
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, of course.

333
00:20:17,535 --> 00:20:17,775
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

334
00:20:18,156 --> 00:20:18,796
[SPEAKER_00]: Not knowing.

335
00:20:19,796 --> 00:20:24,018
[SPEAKER_00]: Like I said, it's like, almost like, it's almost like my questions are... And that's why it doesn't matter the extent.

336
00:20:24,038 --> 00:20:24,618
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you don't...

337
00:20:24,638 --> 00:20:25,718
[SPEAKER_00]: The extent of your learning.

338
00:20:25,738 --> 00:20:25,838
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

339
00:20:25,858 --> 00:20:26,439
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter.

340
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:26,759
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

341
00:20:26,899 --> 00:20:28,199
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's great, if it's small.

342
00:20:28,659 --> 00:20:33,321
[SPEAKER_01]: What matters, basically, is the sense of assumed ownership in regard to it.

343
00:20:33,961 --> 00:20:34,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

344
00:20:34,982 --> 00:20:39,323
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is gratuitous to begin with, but yes, some people invest more in it, some people less.

345
00:20:40,264 --> 00:20:40,524
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

346
00:20:42,905 --> 00:20:44,125
[SPEAKER_01]: So, practically speaking,

347
00:20:44,852 --> 00:20:54,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Physical restraint of your senses, celibacy and so on, not breaking the precepts, is a necessary basis to outline the domain of taking up the body through erection.

348
00:20:55,721 --> 00:21:02,086
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, the verbal restraint of avoiding careless speech, malicious speech, gossip, pointless speech.

349
00:21:02,947 --> 00:21:05,129
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're being silent not because of some, you know...

350
00:21:06,417 --> 00:21:11,842
[SPEAKER_01]: great channeling of some energy or something, it's simply because you're outlining the domain of taking up the mouth.

351
00:21:11,942 --> 00:21:13,223
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the body.

352
00:21:13,423 --> 00:21:15,665
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is, again, a way of taking up the body, exactly.

353
00:21:17,266 --> 00:21:24,252
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, eventually, you can also do that on the level of the mind, whereby your own thoughts and images already are taking up form.

354
00:21:25,934 --> 00:21:28,016
[SPEAKER_01]: I, the body, to that extent.

355
00:21:29,277 --> 00:21:31,158
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's too subtle talk about it now.

356
00:21:31,619 --> 00:21:32,640
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want to confuse people.

357
00:21:33,543 --> 00:21:39,746
[SPEAKER_01]: So, through the physical restraint, you outline the domain of the body that you doubt now you're not engaging.

358
00:21:41,287 --> 00:21:44,808
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the only way to engage with the body domain is to take it up through unwholesome.

359
00:21:45,268 --> 00:21:48,610
[SPEAKER_01]: The only way to engage with the domain of speech is to take it up through unwholesome.

360
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:50,411
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where precepts need to come first.

361
00:21:51,411 --> 00:21:55,113
[SPEAKER_01]: So, practically speaking, in terms of jhāna practice, jhāna development,

362
00:21:56,628 --> 00:22:01,331
[SPEAKER_01]: Physical restraint need to have been done beforehand, but now you start paying attention to your verbal.

363
00:22:01,931 --> 00:22:10,616
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you speak, you only speak when there is a purpose to say something, to the extent that that purpose is expressed, and that's it.

364
00:22:10,896 --> 00:22:16,579
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, then, prevents any engagement of taking up the body carelessly through your mouth.

365
00:22:18,981 --> 00:22:22,643
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more you practice that, the less and less you assume.

366
00:22:23,540 --> 00:22:28,264
[SPEAKER_01]: That ownership of the body through your mouth, through saying, through communicating, and so on.

367
00:22:29,025 --> 00:22:35,150
[SPEAKER_01]: And the less you assume it, the clearer it becomes, its own nature, that it's unassumable, it's unownable.

368
00:22:37,191 --> 00:22:39,093
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's basically the practice of jhāna.

369
00:22:39,113 --> 00:22:48,381
[SPEAKER_01]: So, avoid unnecessary speech, and then use that silence, basically, to discern.

370
00:22:49,460 --> 00:22:57,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, even the extent of the physical mouth that's not speaking, because that's what your body is at the time, that's where your mind is.

371
00:22:58,303 --> 00:22:59,963
[SPEAKER_01]: And then practice not taking that up.

372
00:23:01,884 --> 00:23:02,664
[SPEAKER_01]: And how you take it up?

373
00:23:02,824 --> 00:23:05,225
[SPEAKER_01]: You take up by thinking beyond it, carelessly.

374
00:23:07,445 --> 00:23:12,907
[SPEAKER_01]: Failing to see that whatever you're about to say, it's going to be within the mouth that's been taken up.

375
00:23:13,932 --> 00:23:16,793
[SPEAKER_01]: Not after, not before, not as a result of.

376
00:23:17,393 --> 00:23:17,893
[SPEAKER_01]: It's within.

377
00:23:17,953 --> 00:23:22,254
[SPEAKER_01]: So, take... a mouth taken up is a container of your whole verbal domain.

378
00:23:22,994 --> 00:23:31,675
[SPEAKER_01]: So now, you don't take up the mouth, means you have not taken up or you cannot take up anything, the entire verbal domain, which for you at the time is the bodily domain.

379
00:23:32,615 --> 00:23:35,076
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the sense of safety that comes in the in the first jhāna.

380
00:23:35,116 --> 00:23:37,736
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, the first jhāna is a result of that sense of safety.

381
00:23:38,397 --> 00:23:40,597
[SPEAKER_01]: Safety from sensuality and everything unwholesome.

382
00:23:42,566 --> 00:23:51,888
[SPEAKER_01]: Because physical and verbal, as in your mouth is a very physical thing, it's basically what your body is, for you, practically speaking.

383
00:23:53,228 --> 00:23:57,589
[SPEAKER_01]: What I referred to, that even your thoughts are a way of taking up the form, that's much subtler.

384
00:23:58,309 --> 00:24:03,270
[SPEAKER_01]: And that would not pertain to the same coarseness of the body in terms of sensuality and your will.

385
00:24:06,831 --> 00:24:09,912
[SPEAKER_01]: But yeah, if you stick with the development of the same principle, you would arrive at it.

386
00:24:10,980 --> 00:24:20,624
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's like later on, when the noble disciple frees himself from conceit and all these other subtle things that are not anymore, sort of, expressed through the body.

387
00:24:32,629 --> 00:24:40,653
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you are not speaking, you're practicing silence, as you practice with jhāna, you have thoughts of speaking.

388
00:24:41,508 --> 00:24:43,251
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't try to deny them or remove them.

389
00:24:44,353 --> 00:24:50,582
[SPEAKER_01]: You just now have thoughts of speaking presently and during, and try to not take up the mouth through them.

390
00:24:51,063 --> 00:24:52,044
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let them speak.

391
00:24:53,036 --> 00:24:54,437
[SPEAKER_01]: Without you taking up the mouth.

392
00:24:54,617 --> 00:24:57,318
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, can you say, like, including them within?

393
00:24:57,558 --> 00:24:57,758
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

394
00:24:57,798 --> 00:24:58,298
[SPEAKER_00]: The... Yeah.

395
00:24:58,779 --> 00:24:59,439
[SPEAKER_00]: Not speaking up.

396
00:24:59,459 --> 00:25:01,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Letting them be, basically, is another way of including them.

397
00:25:01,860 --> 00:25:02,100
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

398
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:07,623
[SPEAKER_01]: Including them within, not... Well, including them within the silence that you are doing, for which you're responsible.

399
00:25:08,643 --> 00:25:13,065
[SPEAKER_01]: And you cannot, eh... accidentally break silence.

400
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:16,307
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only choose to be careless and then break the silence.

401
00:25:16,327 --> 00:25:16,427
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

402
00:25:17,370 --> 00:25:22,977
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, if you practice mindfulness of the bodily postures, you cannot accidentally just find yourself standing.

403
00:25:23,297 --> 00:25:25,720
[SPEAKER_01]: You've decided to stand up.

404
00:25:26,301 --> 00:25:33,650
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you're practicing silence, as I said, you only do so to create a container within which you want to include and allow things to be.

405
00:25:34,110 --> 00:25:37,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it's a verbal shouting mind, doesn't matter what it is,

406
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:43,683
[SPEAKER_01]: You know that it doesn't matter how loud it gets, you are the one who chooses to speak as a result of it, and you're not doing that.

407
00:25:44,284 --> 00:25:51,348
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it doesn't matter how much your mindfulness, recollectiveness lapses, it will never lapse for as long as you don't start speaking.

408
00:25:51,948 --> 00:25:53,189
[SPEAKER_01]: It will never completely lapse.

409
00:25:54,890 --> 00:25:59,633
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more you practice that, then, the more familiar you become with what's being included within it.

410
00:25:59,653 --> 00:26:03,575
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the verbal thing... and those things get to get to calm down.

411
00:26:04,256 --> 00:26:07,278
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even your verbal thoughts will calm down, because they're not being expressed.

412
00:26:08,012 --> 00:26:20,162
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, through that, you get to recognize, again, by not taking up the mouth, even on the level of your thought, not just through an act of speech, but even on the level of the thought, well, that quiets them down even more.

413
00:26:20,462 --> 00:26:25,867
[SPEAKER_01]: But you cannot directly tell to your thoughts, be quiet, because you just shouted it out.

414
00:26:27,548 --> 00:26:33,213
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you can think, be quiet, without you taking up the mouth with that thought, that will quiet down the thoughts.

415
00:26:44,877 --> 00:26:45,337
[SPEAKER_00]: Forget that.

416
00:26:46,357 --> 00:26:46,998
[SPEAKER_00]: That last one.

417
00:26:47,018 --> 00:26:47,618
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

418
00:26:49,138 --> 00:26:49,558
[SPEAKER_01]: You can think.

419
00:26:49,598 --> 00:26:50,099
[SPEAKER_01]: Be quiet.

420
00:26:51,019 --> 00:26:51,779
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I said it now.

421
00:26:52,079 --> 00:26:52,359
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

422
00:26:52,619 --> 00:26:53,840
[SPEAKER_01]: If you just think it, don't say it.

423
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:59,941
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you can just think it without even taking up the mouth with that thought.

424
00:27:02,202 --> 00:27:03,923
[SPEAKER_00]: Saying, thinking, be quiet.

425
00:27:04,583 --> 00:27:05,183
[SPEAKER_00]: See, eh...

426
00:27:06,976 --> 00:27:07,917
[SPEAKER_00]: Be quiet, for example.

427
00:27:08,477 --> 00:27:09,278
[SPEAKER_00]: Thought of be quiet.

428
00:27:09,558 --> 00:27:11,099
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind, be quiet.

429
00:27:11,559 --> 00:27:12,260
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an intention.

430
00:27:12,580 --> 00:27:12,820
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

431
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:15,141
[SPEAKER_01]: That you directed towards yourself.

432
00:27:15,422 --> 00:27:15,622
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

433
00:27:15,782 --> 00:27:17,503
[SPEAKER_01]: That you then expressed through that thought.

434
00:27:17,763 --> 00:27:17,983
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

435
00:27:18,223 --> 00:27:22,646
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that direction of quiet is expressed through a thought.

436
00:27:22,786 --> 00:27:22,987
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

437
00:27:23,267 --> 00:27:24,908
[SPEAKER_01]: You took up the mouth and you said it.

438
00:27:25,208 --> 00:27:25,408
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

439
00:27:26,289 --> 00:27:27,089
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't say it.

440
00:27:28,010 --> 00:27:28,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

441
00:27:28,430 --> 00:27:32,493
[SPEAKER_01]: First, you have the thought that is taking up the mouth.

442
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:35,175
[SPEAKER_01]: It's saying to yourself mentally to be quiet.

443
00:27:35,355 --> 00:27:35,555
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

444
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:46,286
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, you can then refine that even further and then just have a thought of the direction of quietude without even taking up the mouth to say it, because you don't need to.

445
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:46,966
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

446
00:27:47,087 --> 00:27:54,111
[SPEAKER_01]: See, taking up the mouth and expressing it is all secondary to the direction that the thought wanted to express, which was already a form of expression.

447
00:27:54,171 --> 00:27:54,431
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

448
00:27:54,471 --> 00:27:55,091
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can't...

449
00:27:55,171 --> 00:28:00,615
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it was only like a further particularization of expression that was already within your thought.

450
00:28:01,530 --> 00:28:05,993
[SPEAKER_01]: But you are used to the level of taking up the mouth or at least saying it.

451
00:28:06,914 --> 00:28:09,896
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, if the person is very unrestrained, doing it physically.

452
00:28:09,956 --> 00:28:10,557
[SPEAKER_00]: What were we saying before?

453
00:28:10,577 --> 00:28:14,280
[SPEAKER_00]: The difference between verbal thoughts and thoughts that aren't verbal thoughts?

454
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:17,122
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, which is the difference between mental intention and verbal intention.

455
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:17,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

456
00:28:19,103 --> 00:28:22,226
[SPEAKER_01]: So, verbal intention is the mental intention that also takes up the mouth.

457
00:28:22,526 --> 00:28:22,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

458
00:28:26,957 --> 00:28:32,444
[SPEAKER_01]: And in the first jhāna, that verbal taking up has subsided.

459
00:28:32,764 --> 00:28:33,685
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you get to think.

460
00:28:34,086 --> 00:28:42,435
[SPEAKER_01]: You get all the directions, all the expressions, without verbalizing it, certainly without speaking, but also without taking up the mouth, which is a basis for speech.

461
00:28:44,477 --> 00:28:47,039
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, yeah, all you need to do is think, be quiet.

462
00:28:47,759 --> 00:28:50,981
[SPEAKER_01]: Not in words, but in the direction of significance of being quiet.

463
00:28:51,041 --> 00:28:51,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

464
00:28:51,661 --> 00:28:54,283
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is container for saying be quiet.

465
00:28:54,463 --> 00:28:54,663
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

466
00:28:54,823 --> 00:28:56,504
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is a container for actually...

467
00:28:56,524 --> 00:28:56,945
[SPEAKER_01]: Speaking.

468
00:28:57,065 --> 00:28:57,485
[SPEAKER_01]: Speaking.

469
00:28:57,645 --> 00:28:58,165
[SPEAKER_01]: Be quiet.

470
00:28:58,265 --> 00:28:58,486
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

471
00:29:01,868 --> 00:29:04,229
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is a container for some sort of physical...

472
00:29:04,389 --> 00:29:05,150
[SPEAKER_01]: Writing it down.

473
00:29:05,210 --> 00:29:05,510
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

474
00:29:05,530 --> 00:29:06,470
[SPEAKER_01]: Having a sign.

475
00:29:06,570 --> 00:29:07,211
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

476
00:29:07,291 --> 00:29:08,792
[SPEAKER_01]: Shouting at others if they're not quiet.

477
00:29:09,092 --> 00:29:10,133
[SPEAKER_01]: Blame or whatever.

478
00:29:10,333 --> 00:29:11,013
[SPEAKER_01]: Getting upset.

479
00:29:11,473 --> 00:29:13,215
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to distract yourself through sensuality.

480
00:29:13,415 --> 00:29:13,675
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

481
00:29:14,997 --> 00:29:17,319
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you didn't get the way you wanted it to be and so on.

482
00:29:21,542 --> 00:29:25,285
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're silent externally, so you get to hear your thoughts.

483
00:29:26,246 --> 00:29:31,570
[SPEAKER_01]: By hearing them, you stop basically verbalizing, you stop taking up the mouth through them.

484
00:29:32,931 --> 00:29:34,672
[SPEAKER_01]: Not by denying them or trying to remove them.

485
00:29:34,792 --> 00:29:35,613
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the point here.

486
00:29:35,933 --> 00:29:36,133
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

487
00:29:36,413 --> 00:29:37,274
[SPEAKER_01]: But by including them.

488
00:29:38,415 --> 00:29:40,957
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they can be without mouth taken up.

489
00:29:42,658 --> 00:29:44,959
[SPEAKER_01]: But mouth taken up cannot be without thoughts.

490
00:29:45,099 --> 00:29:45,239
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

491
00:29:48,101 --> 00:29:52,843
[SPEAKER_01]: But for as long as you're carelessly speaking, habitually taking up the mouth, that's what's first for you.

492
00:29:53,503 --> 00:29:55,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, all the thoughts are secondary, basically, to it.

493
00:29:55,825 --> 00:29:56,325
[SPEAKER_01]: But they're not.

494
00:29:56,405 --> 00:29:57,766
[SPEAKER_01]: They're actually the container of it.

495
00:29:59,647 --> 00:30:02,548
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it always comes down to, like, correcting.

496
00:30:02,568 --> 00:30:03,589
[SPEAKER_00]: Establishing the right order.

497
00:30:03,609 --> 00:30:04,429
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

498
00:30:10,832 --> 00:30:11,973
[SPEAKER_00]: And, essentially, it's...

499
00:30:15,560 --> 00:30:17,862
[SPEAKER_00]: Starting with the body as the container.

500
00:30:18,242 --> 00:30:18,543
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course.

501
00:30:20,044 --> 00:30:21,245
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the principle doesn't change.

